---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FAQItem from '../components/FAQItem.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="FAQ | Static Pulse Sites"
  description="Answers about website development, AI systems, automation, custom internal software, pricing, ownership, and the Static Pulse Sites process."
>
  <main>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Questions about working with Static Pulse Sites.</h1>

        <p class="lead hero-lead">
          You do not need to understand software, automation, or AI before
          contacting us. Start with the business problem, and we will help
          identify the most practical next step.
        </p>

        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">
            Start Your Project
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Services and project fit</h2>

        <FAQItem
          question="What does Static Pulse Sites do?"
          answer="Static Pulse Sites is a Business Systems Studio. We help small and medium businesses improve their websites, connect disconnected tools, automate repetitive work, and build focused internal software."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="How do I know which service I need?"
          answer="You do not need to decide that before contacting us. Explain the process, website, or operational problem you want to improve. We will review the situation and recommend the simplest appropriate solution."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Can the three services be combined?"
          answer="Yes. A project may involve only one service, or it may combine a website, automation, and internal software. For example, a website form could send information into an automated workflow and then update an internal client-management system."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Do you work with specific industries?"
          answer="No. We work with small and medium businesses based on the problems they need to solve rather than their industry."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="What kinds of projects are not a good fit?"
          answer="We are not currently focused on large enterprise platforms, mass-market consumer applications, complex e-commerce ecosystems, or projects that require replacing an entire established software infrastructure."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Process and collaboration</h2>

        <FAQItem
          question="Do I need technical knowledge?"
          answer="No. Our role is to translate the business problem into a practical technical solution. We explain decisions clearly and guide the project without expecting you to understand programming, APIs, automation platforms, or AI models."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="How does a project begin?"
          answer="Projects begin through the contact form. Tell us about your business, the current process or system, and what you want to improve. We will review the information and respond by email with the appropriate next steps."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Will I be involved during the build?"
          answer="Yes. Projects are collaborative. We confirm the problem, review the proposed solution, and gather your feedback during the build instead of waiting until the end."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="How long does a project take?"
          answer="The timeline depends on the scope. A focused website or automation may take a few weeks, while custom software with multiple users, workflows, or integrations may require a longer phased build. The expected timeline is confirmed before work begins."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Do you provide ongoing support?"
          answer="Yes, when required. Support can include website maintenance, workflow monitoring, small improvements, troubleshooting, and continued software development. The support arrangement depends on the system and the level of ongoing involvement needed."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Pricing and ownership</h2>

        <FAQItem
          question="How much does a project cost?"
          answer="Website Development starts at $1,200, AI Systems and Automation starts at $1,000, and Custom Internal Software starts at $2,500. Final pricing depends on the scope, users, features, platforms, integrations, and level of support required."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Why do you show starting prices instead of fixed packages?"
          answer="Automation and software projects vary significantly. Starting prices help visitors understand the general investment level, while the final quote reflects the actual business problem and work required."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Will I own what you build?"
          answer="Yes. Ownership is a core principle of Static Pulse Sites. Clients retain ownership of their website, source code, custom software, and business data, subject to any separate third-party platform terms."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Will I be locked into Static Pulse Sites?"
          answer="No. We want clients to continue working with us because the relationship is useful, not because the system prevents them from leaving. The project structure and ownership model are designed to reduce unnecessary vendor lock-in."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Will I need to pay for third-party tools?"
          answer="Possibly. Some projects require hosting, automation platforms, databases, AI services, email tools, or other software subscriptions. These costs are identified during planning so you understand which expenses belong to third-party services and which belong to Static Pulse Sites."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Websites, AI, and software</h2>

        <FAQItem
          question="Do you only build static websites?"
          answer="Static architecture remains our preferred approach for many informational websites because it is fast, reliable, and low maintenance. However, the correct website structure depends on the business requirements and any forms, portals, integrations, or dynamic features involved."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Do you add AI to every project?"
          answer="No. AI is used only when it provides practical value. Many problems are better solved with clear processes, straightforward automation, or traditional software."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Can you connect tools we already use?"
          answer="Yes, when the tools support suitable integrations or APIs. We review your existing platforms before recommending replacements because the simplest solution is often to improve how current systems work together."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Can you build a custom CRM or portal?"
          answer="Yes. We build focused internal systems such as CRMs, client portals, onboarding tools, dashboards, document systems, and operational trackers when existing software does not support the process cleanly."
        />

        <FAQItem
          question="Is any website or software completely secure?"
          answer="No responsible provider should promise absolute security. We reduce unnecessary dependencies, apply appropriate safeguards, and design systems with security in mind, but every system still requires proper access controls, configuration, maintenance, and responsible use."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="cta-box">
          <h2>Still unsure where to begin?</h2>

          <p class="lead">
            Describe what is not working, what your team currently uses, and
            what you want the business to do more efficiently.
          </p>

          <div class="button-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">
              Start Your Project
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>